window.GAGARIN_SEARCH = [{"title":"Archive of Roman Gagarin's work — advertising and marketing | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/archive/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 07 / SARATOV ARCHIVE for the meticulous Here I have gathered my early projects, my work with Saratov companies and my old professional profiles. I don't throw the past away just because today I do other things. TO HOME PAGE ↗ INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU First jobs October 2017 — June 2019 \"Teleport\" · Head of Advertising and PR At Teleport I worked on advertising campaigns, websites, SMM, contextual advertising and events. I managed the work of a content manager, a Direct specialist and freelancers. I also took on tasks that did not fit within the job title. Specialist catalogue June 2019 — July 2020 “GagarinFoto” · Commercial Director At GagarinFoto I ran my own photo services studio. I was responsible for commercial work and the day-to-day running of the business. In a role like that, you can't simply say “that's not my job.” August — November 2019 Di-Center Medical · Marketing Lead At Di-Center I was responsible for the marketing plan, a team of five, contractors, the budget, analytics and reporting. The job meant not only coming up with promotion, but also organising people and the work itself. Specfinder lists the period as 2019–2020, while my résumé says August–November 2019. The old records don't fully match, so I've kept both dates. Specialist catalogue Early Projects 2020 · Game Project “Operator 911” “Operator 911” is my early text-based chat horror game and my first attempt at crowdfunding on Planeta.ru. I wrote a separate article about how I made the project and what happened with the funds raised. Open project page ↗ Publication · 2020 Indie Crowdfunding in Russia In this piece I go through my own experience launching a small game: how I looked for an audience, how I tried crowdfunding, and what results I got. Article on DTF ↗ · Planeta.ru archive ↗ How the archive works The main selection includes the projects I want to present myself with now. Earlier work remains available here in case anyone needs additional context. Not every old experiment is a current product or an up-to-date service. Archived Profiles and Service Catalogues I've kept my old profiles from professional platforms here. The services and prices listed in them don't necessarily match what I offer now. Services and Portfolio Specfinder My old professional questionnaire with entries on “Teleport” and Di-Center. GagarinRO2 Questionnaire Freelance Platform Kwork My old profile on Kwork under the name Gagarin64. The services and prices in it date from that time. Open profile Full Professional Timeline My full work history, books and current projects are collected in the biography. Professional Experience"},{"title":"Dvigat Indi — Roman Gagarin's book on promoting games","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/books/dvigat-indi/","section":"Book","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 06 / BOOK / SARATOV Dvigat Indi Marketing for Independent Video Games ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU LIBRARY / BYGAGARIN Author's Book · 2025 Here I've left information about the book and links to where you can find it. ← ALL BOOKS About the Book In “Dvigat Indi” I wrote about things I have run into many times in game development and marketing: how to find an audience, how to explain what you are making, and how to reach video bloggers, journalists and gaming communities. About the Edition Author Roman Gagarin Publishing System Ridero Release Date 6 February 2025 Length 148 pages · via Ridero ISBN 978-5-0065-4193-1 Formats Print book; EPUB, FB2, PDF, MOBI Ridero Publisher Listing Where It's Published Ridero Yandex Books The length of the book may differ between platforms. I took the date and page count here from the publisher's listing. Author's Materials Excerpt and ISBN on MyBook Author page with EPUB Book announcement · 09.02.2025 All Books"},{"title":"Books by Roman Gagarin — marketing and indie development","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/books/","section":"Book","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 06 / SARATOV BOOKS To the point I've written three books: on low-cost advertising, small business marketing, and promoting independent games. These are subjects I have worked on myself and continue to work on. TO HOME PAGE ↗ INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU Advertising for Pennies 30 proven ways In the first book I collected low-cost ways to advertise: partnerships, customer referrals, gifts and choosing the right platforms. For situations where there is simply no big budget. 16 August 2017 · 52 pp. via Ridero · ISBN 978-5-4485-5503-9 Publication card About the book ↗ Marketing for the Broke Simple, cheap, clear I wrote “Marketing for the Poor” for small businesses: positioning, customers, advertising and promotion, for when money is tight but the work still has to get done. 27 June 2018 · 94 pp. via Ridero · ISBN 978-5-4493-0656-2 Publication card About the book ↗ Dvigat Indi Marketing for Independent Video Games “Moving Indie” is my book about promoting a small game: finding an audience, talking about the project, and working with video platforms and communities. 6 February 2025 · 148 pp. via Ridero · ISBN 978-5-0065-4193-1 Publication card About the book ↗"},{"title":"Marketing for the Poor — a book by Roman Gagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/books/marketing-dlya-bednykh/","section":"Book","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 06 / BOOK / SARATOV Marketing for the Broke Simple, cheap, clear ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU LIBRARY / BYGAGARIN Author’s book · 2018 Here I've left information about the book and links to where you can find it. ← ALL BOOKS About the Book I wrote “Marketing for the Poor” for people who build or grow a small business. I cover advertising, positioning, working with clients and promotion methods when the budget is limited. About the Edition Author Roman Gagarin Publishing System Ridero Release Date 27 June 2018 Length 94 pages · via Ridero ISBN 978-5-4493-0656-2 Formats Print book; EPUB, FB2, PDF, MOBI Ridero Publisher Listing Where It's Published Ridero Yandex Books The length of the book may differ between platforms. I took the date and page count here from the publisher's listing. All Books"},{"title":"Advertising for Pennies — a book by Roman Gagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/books/reklama-za-kopeiki/","section":"Book","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 06 / BOOK / SARATOV Advertising for Pennies 30 proven ways ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU LIBRARY / BYGAGARIN Author’s book · 2017 Here I've left information about the book and links to where you can find it. ← ALL BOOKS About the Book I released “Advertising for Pennies” in 2017. I collected ways to promote a small business without serious investment: partnerships, referrals, gifts for customers and advertising platforms. About the Edition Author Roman Gagarin Publishing System Ridero Release Date 16 August 2017 Length 52 pages · via Ridero ISBN 978-5-4485-5503-9 Formats Print book; EPUB, FB2, PDF, MOBI Ridero Publisher Listing Where It's Published Ridero Yandex Books The length of the book may differ between platforms. I took the date and page count here from the publisher's listing. All Books"},{"title":"Marketing calculators: ROI, ROMI, CAC, LTV — byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/calculators/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / MARKETING / NUMBERS CALCULATORS for work. I’ve collected here the things I constantly need to calculate myself: advertising, profit, payback, sales, customers and project economics. Enter the numbers and see the result right away. No registration, no data sent to a server. All calculations run directly in your browser. Empty denominators are shown as a dash, not as zero or infinity. Formulas for each calculation are shown openly. Forecasts are scenarios under the stated conditions. TO MY TOOLS ↗ 01 / 16 Advertising funnel CTR, CPM, CPC, CPL, CAC, conversions and ROAS from a single set of numbers. Formula: CTR = clicks / impressions × 100%; CPL = ad budget / leads; CAC = budget / sales; ROAS = revenue / budget. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 02 / 16 ROI — return on investment How much the project earned or lost after all the listed expenses. Formula: ROI = (revenue − all costs) / all costs × 100%. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 03 / 16 ROMI — return on marketing investment Accounts for sales margin: I don’t confuse revenue with earned money. Formula: ROMI = (revenue × margin − marketing costs) / marketing costs × 100%. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 04 / 16 Profit and profitability What is left after variable, fixed and marketing costs. Formula: Profit = revenue − variable − fixed − marketing costs. Profitability = profit / revenue × 100%. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 05 / 16 Margin and markup I check the price of a product or service and don’t confuse margin with markup. Formula: Margin = (price − cost price) / price × 100%; markup = (price − cost price) / cost price × 100%. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 06 / 16 Break-even point How many units must be sold to cover fixed costs. Formula: Units = round up [fixed costs / (price − variable cost per unit)]. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 07 / 16 Revenue for target profit Reverse calculation: how much must be earned to cover costs and reach the goal. Formula: Revenue = (fixed costs + desired profit) / contribution margin ratio. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 08 / 16 Discount and its consequences How much will need to be sold after a discount to keep the same gross profit. Formula: New price = price × (1 − discount); required volume = old gross profit / new profit per unit. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 09 / 16 LTV — customer value A simple model of revenue and gross profit over the entire customer relationship. Formula: LTV by gross profit = average check × purchases per year × years of relationship × margin. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 10 / 16 LTV to CAC ratio I compare the gross profit from a customer with the cost of acquiring them. Formula: LTV / CAC = customer gross profit over the period / cost of acquiring them. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 11 / 16 ARPU and ARPPU Average revenue per user and per paying user. Formulas: ARPU = revenue / active users; ARPPU = revenue / paying users. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 12 / 16 Customer churn What share of the client base left during the period and how many remain. Formula: Churn = clients lost / clients at the start of the period × 100%. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 13 / 16 CAC payback period How many months of gross profit from a client it takes to cover the cost of acquiring them. Formula: Months = CAC / (monthly revenue per client × margin). For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 14 / 16 Media plan by CPM Budget for the given impressions and a scenario forecast of clicks and leads. Formulas: Budget = impressions / 1000 × CPM; clicks = impressions × CTR; leads = clicks × conversion rate. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 15 / 16 How many clicks and how much money A plan worked backwards from a sales target, through conversion rates and CPC. Formula: Clicks = sales / (click-to-lead conversion × lead-to-sale conversion); budget = clicks × CPC. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. 16 / 16 Savings from automation Time is money too: what the process costs and when automation pays for itself. Formula: Monthly savings = hours × cost per hour; payback period = implementation cost / monthly savings. For the interactive calculation, enable JavaScript. The formula is shown above. Want to test an unusual task or build a calculation like this into your own service? Write to me . Or see what I work with ."},{"title":"Consent to the processing of personal data — byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/consent/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / LEGAL INFORMATION CONSENT to data processing A separate consent to send a request through the byGagarin form. NABERUSHKIN ROMAN OLEGOVICH · NPD (self-employed) Revision of 18 November 2026. 1. Operator Consent is given to the individual Roman Olegovich Naberushkin , who applies the special tax regime “Tax on Professional Income” (self-employed), contact address: gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru . 2. What the consent covers The user freely, of their own will and in their own interest, gives a separate consent to the processing of the personal data that they voluntarily include in a request prepared on the byGagarin website and sent by them independently to the operator by email or via Telegram. Such data may include name, email address, username or profile name on Telegram, other contact details, the content of the request and correspondence, information about the task, and files voluntarily attached by the user. Do not include passport details, health information, biometric data, bank details, or data of third parties in the request unless there is a separate lawful basis for doing so. 3. Purposes of processing to receive and review the request; to reply to the user and, if necessary, to clarify the circumstances of the task; to prepare a proposal, discuss terms, and conclude a contract. This consent does not extend to marketing mailings, publication of reviews, distribution of data, or transfer of data for independent marketing by third parties. 4. Actions and methods of processing The operator may collect, record, systematise, accumulate, store, update, use, block, delete, and destroy the data provided. Processing may be carried out with or without automated means, in email correspondence and in other forms necessary for the stated purposes. 5. Term and withdrawal The consent is valid until the purposes of processing are achieved, but no longer than 12 months from the date of the last substantive contact, if no contract has been concluded and there are no other lawful grounds for storing the data. If a contract is concluded, the data may continue to be processed to the extent and for the period necessary to perform it and to comply with the requirements of the law. Consent may be withdrawn by letter to gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru with the subject “Withdrawal of consent to the processing of personal data”. After receiving the withdrawal, the operator stops processing based on consent and destroys the data, unless their further storage is required on another lawful basis, within the time limits set by Article 21 of Federal Law No. 152-FZ. 6. How consent is confirmed on the website On the contacts page, consent is requested through a separate checkbox that is not pre-ticked and is not combined with confirmation of having read the Privacy Policy. After the checkbox is ticked, the text of the separate consent is added as an independent block to the generated brief. The website does not send the brief automatically: the user opens an email app themselves or copies the text and sends it through the channel of their choice. The operator receives the message and the confirmation text it contains only after the user sends it independently. If the user has only generated the text in the browser and has not sent it to the operator, the operator receives neither the brief itself nor any information about the checkbox being ticked. Personal data processing policy: open document . Operator: Naberushkin Roman Olegovich · gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru ."},{"title":"Roman Gagarin (Naberushkin) — biography and experience | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/experience/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BIOGRAPHY no legends I am Roman Gagarin. In documents, I am Roman Olegovich Naberushkin. I am a marketer and developer of digital products from Saratov. I work at the intersection of marketing, PR, SEO, product management, and the development of my own games, websites, and tools. Work experience This is my work history, from advertising in Saratov to game products and my own projects. My job titles did not always describe everything I did: I worked with people, processes and all kinds of tasks. Some jobs overlapped, and I have kept the dates as they appear in my CV. Teleport October 2017 — June 2019 Head of Advertising and PR At Teleport I led advertising and PR, and handled websites, SMM, contextual advertising, events and contractors. This was work with people and day-to-day tasks, not just ad accounts. Advertising campaigns from concept to delivery; market and competitor analysis. SMM, search advertising, project websites, events and news hooks. Led and mentored a content manager, a search advertising specialist and freelancers; developed marketing materials. My old Specfinder profile lists my position as PR Director, for the period 2017–2019. Specfinder profile GagarinFoto June 2019 — July 2020 Commercial Director At GagarinFoto I looked after the commercial side of my own photo studio. When a business is small and your own, you are responsible not for a nice sign on the door, but for making sure everything works. I have kept this period and title as they appear in my CV. Medical Di-Center August — November 2019 Head of Marketing At Di-Center I was responsible for the marketing plan, the team, contractors, budget and reporting. I dealt not only with advertising but also with how all of it was organised internally. Built the marketing plan and budget. Tracked tasks for a team of five and coordinated contractors. Analysed results and prepared reports. My old Specfinder profile gives the period 2019–2020 and the title “head of advertising department.” My CV says August–November 2019. I am keeping both versions, because old profiles and the timeline do not always match. Specfinder profile Volga Studios December 2019 — February 2023 CMO / Product PR Manager / Product Manager At Volga Studios I was responsible for marketing, PR and product. I prepared the Kickstarter, worked with the press, took part in developing the game itself, and handled organisational matters, including office admin duties when the team needed them. Developed strategic and detailed marketing plans to build awareness of the game. Prepared and ran the Kickstarter campaign; worked with the press. My comment about the game was published by DSOGaming and Twinfinite in April 2021. They listed me as Community Manager, which reflects one real side of my work with the team and its audience. DSOGaming · 07.04.2021 Twinfinite · 07.04.2021 Podcast · 18.02.2020 Apriori Furniture Factory September 2023 — July 2024 Head of Digital Marketing At Apriori I led digital marketing: SEO, websites, advertising budgets, contractors, bots, and work with a network of showrooms. As usual, the tasks went well beyond a single advertising channel. Built promotional websites on Tilda and handled SEO for the company’s websites. Consolidated information about the showroom network across Russia and the CIS; worked with reviews. Managed the digital advertising budget, social targeting and tasks for search advertising specialists. Developed and launched Telegram and WhatsApp bots for customer communication; coordinated contractors and controlled quality. Dates and responsibilities are taken from my CV. Hotel Areal From August 2024 · period from my 2025 CV Marketer At Hotel Areal I worked on marketing strategy, SEO, contextual advertising, the website, VK Ads and reporting. Here too I had to connect different channels into one working system. Coordinated search advertising and SEO contractors; set tasks and wrote briefs. Built development strategies, maintained the website and kept its content up to date. Set up VK targeting and prepared monthly reports across marketing channels. This is how the period is recorded in my CV dated 14 May 2025. It is a record of my work, not a statement about my current position. First books and advertising In 2017 I published “Advertising for Pennies,” my first book, about promotion without large budgets. By then I was already working on my own projects and running an advertising agency, which I describe in my author bio with the publisher. Ridero · author bio Education Saratov State University named after N. G. Chernyshevsky, Social Work. 2020 . Development talk On 18 February 2020, an interview with me about “The Emperor’s Own” and the work of our team was released. In April 2021, my comment on the alpha demo was published by foreign game press, where I was listed as Community Manager. Igrozhory DSOGaming Twinfinite Skills and tools Marketing strategy, campaign planning and competitor PR analysis. Yandex Direct, social targeting, SEO, brand promotion and product launches. Team, project and budget management; regional and nationwide advertising campaigns. Russian: native. English: B1 in the May 2025 CV. Download CV · PDF (Russian) Original HH.ru CV, updated 14 May 2025. The PDF is in Russian and describes that period. Own projects 2025–2026 I am currently developing SNG Games, All Indie, Panorama Studio, my own games, Windows programs, and I write books, including “Moving Indie.” The ideas, product decisions, content and final results are mine; in implementation and code review I work actively with AI. My projects ↗ Moving Indie ↗ About All Indie ↗"},{"title":"Roman Gagarin, marketer and developer in Saratov | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/","section":"Page","priority":12,"text":"ROMAN GAGARIN / SARATOV / 2026 I TAKE ON TASKS, NOT LABELS . I am Roman Gagarin. I work in marketing, PR and SEO, and I build websites, games and various digital tools. I live in Saratov and work with projects across Russia. HOW I SOLVE PROBLEMS ↗ MY WORK ↘ WHERE TO START WITH? Here are my projects, tools and texts. Start with whatever interests you, or use search. 01 / SOLUTIONS Come with a problem, not a service name ↗ 02 / WORK Games, websites, catalogs, campaigns ↗ 03 / BIOGRAPHY Who I am, where I'm from, where I've worked and what I've done ↗ 04 / LAB I won't explain it, you can try it ↗ 05 / WRITING Books, publications, interviews, archive ↗ 06 / CALCULATORS ROI, ROMI, funnel, profit and 12 more calculations ↗ NOT WORDS. HERE IT IS. A game catalog, a horror game about an elevator, and a file utility. Three completely different things I built. You can look at each one. MEDIA / CATALOG LIVE PROJECT ↗ SELECTED / 01 SNG GAMES SNG Games is my media project and catalogue of CIS games. News, game cards, releases, search, and the publishing system I built. OPEN CASE ↗ WEBSITES, GAMES AND TOOLS FULL CATALOGUE ↗ IN-HOUSE TOOL / 360° GAGARIN PANORAMA STUDIO. Panorama Studio is my editor for interactive 360° spaces. Scenes, transitions, objects, events. You can try it in the browser; if you need it for your project, we can discuss it separately. ABOUT THE PRODUCT ↗ OPEN DEMO ↗ DISCUSS A LICENCE ↗ THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK VARIOUS PROJECTS. ONE AUTHOR. I'm from Saratov. I work at the intersection of marketing, PR and product management; I build websites, games and software, develop game media and write books. In development I work a lot with AI. I come up with ideas, set tasks, decide what should work and how, and check the results. AI helps with code, assembly and routine work. The finished things I show here, and you can open and try them. My professional experience includes leading advertising and PR at Teleport, a marketing team of five at Medical Di-Center, digital marketing at Apriori and marketing and product work at Volga Studios. READ THE BIOGRAPHY ↗ Download CV · PDF (Russian) 01 / BIOGRAPHY Biography and experience ↗ 02 / LIBRARY Books ↗ 03 / PRESS Publications and interviews ↗ 04 / ARCHIVE Where it all started ↗ YES HAVE A PROBLEM? Not sure where to start? Tell me what you want to do or where you're stuck. We'll go through your brief and work out how I can help. ROMAN GAGARIN Marketer and developer · Saratov ↗ SARATOV · PROJECTS ACROSS RUSSIA"},{"title":"Marketer in Saratov: strategy, PR, SEO and advertising | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/marketing-saratov/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"MARKETING in Saratov I'm Roman Gagarin, a marketer from Saratov. I work on strategy, audits, PR, SEO, contextual and targeted advertising, content and analytics. I take on projects in Saratov and remotely across Russia. 01 / Task First, understand what is holding back growth. I don't think marketing work is just setting up ads. I'm interested in the whole system: the product itself, the people it's made for, the offer, customer acquisition, and what happens after the first contact. 01 Audit · Strategy · Positioning Unclear who the product is for and why it's needed I analyse the audience, competitors, offer and customer journey. I help formulate positioning, set priorities and build a realistic promotion plan. Audit of marketing, website and acquisition channels Research of audience and competitive environment Positioning, UVP and marketing strategy Media plan, budget and measurable KPIs Result: a clear picture of the current situation, priorities and an action plan. 02 Internet marketing · SEO · Advertising You need enquiries, not just traffic I work with search promotion, advertising and content. I look not only at clicks, but also at what happens after the visit: an enquiry, a request, a purchase or a bounce. SEO audit and organic traffic growth Contextual and targeted advertising SMM, content plan and community work Funnel, conversion and ad budget analytics Result: linking acquisition channels, the website and analytics with clear performance criteria. 03 PR · Media · Communications The project should be known and properly understood I help build a public image for a product: from shaping its story and press materials to making contact with editors, bloggers and relevant communities. PR strategy and communications plan Working with journalists, bloggers and industry media Press releases, articles, interviews and content Promoting launches and independent projects Result: consistent communication and materials that explain the value of the product. 04 Product · Games · Independent development A product needs to reach the market A separate area of my work is marketing for games and digital products. I take into account the specifics of indie development, small teams, limited budgets and the long cycle of building a product. Positioning and presentation of a game product Launch plan, audience and promotion channels Working with game media and communities Preparing campaigns and materials for crowdfunding Result: a promotion plan that matches the development stage and the team’s real resources. Volga Studios case ↗ 02 / Practice Experience you can verify. Marketing and PR have been my profession for many years. I have worked in them at Saratov companies, a game studio and my own projects. Here I show not a list of fine words, but what I have actually worked on. 01 Volga Studios · 2019–2023 CMO / PR / Product At Volga Studios I was responsible for marketing and PR and took part in developing the game The Emperor’s Own itself. I prepared the Kickstarter, dealt with the press and handled organisational matters too. The campaign reached 229 backers and $32,739 in pledged contributions against a goal of $100,000, and was then cancelled. It was not a successful raise, but it was serious hands-on experience. Case breakdown and sources ↗ 02 Advertising · Marketing · Digital Work with companies and teams At Teleport I ran advertising and PR, at Di-center I led marketing, and at Apriori I headed the digital direction. At Volga Studios I worked on marketing, product and press at the same time. Almost everywhere, the real scope of work was wider than the official job title. I have kept the full chronology in my biography. Teleport — led Advertising and PR from October 2017 to June 2019: campaigns, SMM, websites, events and mentoring the team. Medical Di-Center — Head of Marketing, August–November 2019: a team of five, planning, contractors, budget and reports. Apriori furniture factory — Head of Digital Marketing, September 2023–July 2024: Tilda, SEO, advertising budgets, showroom information across Russia and the CIS, reviews and customer bots. Hotel Areal — role recorded from August 2024 in the May 2025 CV: advertising and SEO contractors, VK targeting, website management and monthly reporting. Full biography and chronology ↗ 03 Books · Publications · Own media Marketing is also a subject of my own writing I write about low-cost advertising, promoting small projects and marketing independent games. I develop SNG Games and create my own products, on which I test editorial and product approaches. Books ↗ Publications and interviews ↗ SNG Games ↗ 03 / Format No promises no magic button. I prefer to understand the business and do the work, rather than sell attractive promises. First I look at what already works, where money is being lost and which tasks are actually worth tackling first. 01 Analyse Diagnostics Goals, product, audience, website, competitors, channels and analytics. We separate real problems from assumptions. 02 Define Strategy and plan We set priorities, tasks, channels, budget, roles and metrics. We agree on exactly what we count as a result. 03 Execute Implementation and control We launch the agreed work, test hypotheses, look at the numbers and adjust our actions. 04 / Geography Saratov. All of Russia. I live and work in Saratov. I take on tasks from local companies and teams, and I work remotely with projects from other regions. If you need a marketer in Saratov or help with PR, SEO and product promotion, tell me what is going on. You don’t have to choose a service in advance. We’ll work out the right approach based on the task. Meeting address by prior arrangement: Saratov, Bolshaya Sadovaya St., 141"},{"title":"Personal data processing policy — byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/privacy/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / LEGAL INFORMATION POLICY personal data What data the website processes, why, where it arises and how the user can manage it. NABERUSHKIN ROMAN OLEGOVICH · NPD (self-employed) Revision of 18 November 2026. 1. Operator and scope Personal data operator: Naberushkin Roman Olegovich , an individual applying the special tax regime “Tax on Professional Income” (self-employed). Contact for questions about the processing of personal data: gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru . This policy applies to the byGagarin website and to messages that the user chooses to send to the operator by email or via Telegram. It describes how the website actually works as of the revision date and does not mean that the website automatically receives or stores every form submission. 2. What data is processed Message text: the selected direction, task description, desired outcome, and any details the user includes in the message. Sender data: name and email address shown when a message is received; profile name and Telegram username if the message is sent via messenger; other contact details voluntarily provided in the message. Correspondence and attachments: the content of replies and files that the user has sent to the operator. Hosting technical data: when visiting GitHub Pages, the hosting service itself may log the visitor's IP address for security purposes. According to GitHub's documentation, such IP addresses are recorded and stored by GitHub; the site operator does not receive these logs through the form or the site interface. More details: GitHub Pages documentation and GitHub privacy statement . The operator does not request passport details, health information, biometric data, bank details, or special categories of personal data through the form. Do not include such information in the task description. Do not send other people's data without a lawful basis. 3. How the form on the site works The form on the site is a brief text generator. The selected direction, task description, and desired outcome are processed by a script directly in the user's browser. The site has no server-side form handler, user account area, or database of requests, and the completed fields are not sent to the operator automatically. After the brief is generated, the user decides what to do next: open the prepared email, copy the text and send it by email themselves, or paste it into Telegram. Transfer to the operator happens only when the user sends the message. Until then, the form values remain in the current browser page. 4. Purposes and legal grounds for processing Replying to a message, clarifying the task, preparing a proposal, and negotiating a contract. Basis: actions taken at the request of the data subject to conclude a contract and, after conclusion, performance of the contract (clause 5, part 1, article 6 of Federal Law No. 152-FZ), as well as the user's separate consent where it is requested through the form. Fulfilling obligations established by law. Basis: the relevant provisions of the legislation of the Russian Federation, including when drawing up and performing a contract and keeping mandatory records. Protecting the operator's rights and legitimate interests. Processing correspondence and information related to a message may be necessary to confirm agreements and protect rights within the limits permitted by law. The data is not used for automated decisions that produce legal consequences for the user, and is not used for marketing mailings without a separate legal basis. 5. Processing activities and services used After a message is received, the operator may collect, review, organise, clarify, use, store, restrict, and delete the personal data it contains, only to the extent necessary for the stated purposes. Email: messages are accepted at the address gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru . Delivery and storage of email correspondence also depend on the email services of the sender and recipient, which follow their own rules. Telegram: if the user chooses this channel, messages pass through the Telegram service. Telegram processes data in accordance with its own privacy policy . The operator does not control this service's infrastructure or its independent processing of data. GitHub Pages: is used to host the site. Technical security logs of the hosting service are processed by GitHub under its own rules. The operator does not sell personal data, pass it to advertising networks, or instruct third parties to send advertising. Disclosure to state authorities is possible only in cases and in the manner provided by law. 6. Cookies and local storage As of the revision date, the byGagarin site code does not use cookies, web analytics systems, advertising pixels, or behavioural tracking tools. For this reason, no separate consent banner for advertising or analytics cookies is set on the site. To remember the interface accessibility setting, namely the choice of reduced motion, the site uses the browser's local storage ( localStorage ) with the key gagarin-reduced-motion . This value is stored in the user's browser, is not sent to the operator, and is not used to identify the visitor. It can be deleted in the browser's site data settings. This description does not override the independent processing of technical data by the hosting provider, described in section 2. 7. Retention periods If a message does not lead to a contract, the correspondence and related data are kept for no longer than 12 months from the date of the last substantive contact, after which they are deleted unless another legal basis for further storage exists. If a contract is concluded, documents and information are kept for as long as necessary to perform the contract, meet legal requirements, and protect the parties' rights. GitHub Pages technical logs are stored by GitHub itself in accordance with its own rules and retention periods; the site operator does not manage these logs. 8. User rights and requests The user may request information about the processing of their personal data, demand its correction, restriction, or destruction where legally permitted grounds exist, and withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. To do so, send an email to gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru with the subject “Personal data”. Indicate which message the request relates to so the operator can locate the relevant correspondence. Withdrawing consent does not stop processing if another legal basis for it remains. The time limits for ending processing and destroying data are set by article 21 of Federal Law No. 152-FZ. 9. Data protection The operator takes necessary and sufficient organisational and technical measures to protect received data from unlawful access, alteration, disclosure, restriction, copying, and destruction. Access to correspondence is limited to the person handling the relevant request. Data must not be used for purposes incompatible with those for which it was provided. 10. Changes to this policy The current version is published on this page. If the form changes, analytics are added, new services are introduced, requests are stored on a server, or data is handled in any other new way, the policy must be updated before that processing begins. Operator contact: Naberushkin Roman Olegovich · gagarinfoto64@yandex.ru · @gagarin64ru ."},{"title":"All Indie — catalogue of independent games and digital projects | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/all-indie/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV All Indie A catalogue of independent games, utilities, and digital projects. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 02 DIRECTION: Catalogue · Own project ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project I built All Indie as my own platform for games, programs, websites, and experiments. I did not want to simply pile links into a list. What matters to me is that a person quickly understands what the project is, and can open it and try it right away. I develop and maintain the site and catalogue. I built the project cards, categories, search and direct launch links. This is where I publish my own developments and independent digital products. View the work Open All Indie ↗ Project catalogue ↗ Support the author ↗ Authorship and additional work On All Indie I collect my own games and programmes. They are split into two selections here, so you can choose what to try. About the author of All Indie Games and experiments Utilities and extensions"},{"title":"Browser games and experiments — Roman Gagarin | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/browser-games/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Browser games and experiments Additional published games, game prototypes and interactive works. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 10 DIRECTION: Author projects · byGagarin ← FULL CATALOGUE Author selection Here I have gathered my browser games from All Indie. Some are short, finished pieces, and others are projects I keep working on. You can open any game right away and try it. The author on his projects One Ordinary Day I made an interactive story in which time changes along with your decisions. Published browser version · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Atlas of Zero I came up with a game about an encyclopedia, where correcting an article changes reality itself. Published browser version · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Matrix Operator I experimented with a digital system into whose life you can interfere and observe the consequences. Operator Loop 2.3 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ White Silence I built a survival game in a winter valley: you manage supplies, keep warm and restore radio contact. Browser · PC · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Reseller.exe I made a game about the used car market: inspections, hidden defects, repairs and haggling. Local build 2.3 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Durak with O. Zh. Grant My “Durak” is a match against the computer with saving in the browser. Published browser version · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Light Catch I built an arcade game about intercepting impulses, with upgrades between shifts. Local release 1.0 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ SITE.exe I made a clicker about developing a website: upgrades, growth and passive income. Local release 1.4 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Delete for Everyone I experimented with horror inside a fictional messenger. Standalone browser build 1.0 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ B-Movie Shooter I built a top-down shooter with a campaign and a survival mode. Beta 1.0.3 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ The Last Pass I made a story about checking documents at a quarantine checkpoint. What happens depends on your decisions. Local release 1.0.2 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Matter — Generative Study 001 My procedural graphics with sound synthesised directly in the browser. Generative experiment 001 · author project by byGagarin About the game ↗ Play ↗ Hollywood Massacre: development diary In my diary on DEV I write about working on the browser shooter Hollywood Massacre: enemy behaviour, levels and performance. A standalone build under this name has not been published yet. DEV Community diary"},{"title":"National platform of digital products — byGagarin concept","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/digital-platform-initiative/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV National platform of digital products in Russia A proposal for the infrastructure of the market for digital materials and tools in Russia. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 13 DIRECTION: Analytics · Initiative concept ← FULL CATALOGUE About the document I proposed a shared platform for digital products in Russia: code, templates, graphics, game assets and other materials. I worked out the catalogue, search, author profiles, file access and the organisational model. Public concept Role and status I put the concept of such a platform into a separate document: how it is structured, what authors receive and how users find products. This is my proposal, not an announcement that the platform has already launched. About the concept ↗ Materials In the repository I published the concept, the roadmap, the economic model and the sources. Source files and documents ↗ Published version"},{"title":"The Emperor’s Own — Marketing and Kickstarter Case by Roman Gagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/emperors-own/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV «The Emperor’s Own» The Emperor's Own is a story-driven RPG set in an alternate 19th-century Russian Empire. My working case study on marketing a game product and preparing a Kickstarter campaign. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 01 DIRECTION: Volga Studios · Saratov · CMO / PR / Product ← FULL CATALOGUE I worked on The Emperor’s Own at Volga Studios: product, marketing, PR, Kickstarter and the day-to-day operations of a small studio. The campaign drew 229 backers and $32 739 in pledged contributions against a goal of $100 000. The funding did not succeed — the campaign was cancelled. Advertising cost around 5 000 ₽, as far as I remember. My role From December 2019 to February 2023 I worked at Volga Studios in Saratov. On paper I was CMO, product PR manager and Product Manager. In practice I dealt not only with promotion but with the product itself. When something in a small studio needed solving, I could be both organiser and office manager. Job titles only describe part of what I did. I built the strategy and detailed promotion plans for game products. I prepared and ran the Kickstarter crowdfunding campaign. I communicated with the game press, prepared materials and presented the game to audiences. This was work not only with advertising but with the game itself. My involvement is visible in publications from those years. I left the full timeline in my biography. Full timeline Campaign We launched the Kickstarter on 4 November 2020; it was scheduled to end on 3 January 2021. Kicktraq still holds the figures: 229 backers, $32 739 in pledged contributions against a goal of $100 000 — about 32.7% of the planned amount. The campaign was later cancelled. We did not reach the goal. But over the course of the work we found 229 backers, received attention from the international press, showed the game to audiences and took plenty of hard knocks. For me this is part of real product work, not a line on a résumé. About the project At Volga Studios we made The Emperor’s Own, a story-driven adventure with RPG elements. An alternate early 19th-century empire, a secret intelligence officer, decisions with consequences for history. I was inside the work on the game product, not just someone who was supposed to advertise it. On 4 November 2020 we released The Emperor’s Own: Alpha Teaser on Steam for free. It still lists Volga Studios as developer and publisher. You can open the page and see what we showed players. Steam listing: developer and date Campaign and publications Kickstarter page ↗ Pledge and date archive ↗ Game page on Steam ↗ Announcement on DTF · 05.11.2020 ↗ Rozetked · 05.11.2020 ↗ CoreMission · 06.11.2020 ↗ Podcast “Igrozhory” · 18.02.2020 ↗ My comments in the foreign press On 7 April 2021 DSOGaming and Twinfinite wrote about the alpha teaser and published my comment on behalf of Volga Studios. In these articles I am listed as Roman Naberushkin, Community Manager. This is how I presented the game and the team to the foreign press. John Papadopoulos for DSOGaming and Alex Gibson for Twinfinite wrote about the game. Both used my comment. The articles are linked below. DSOGaming · 07.04.2021 Twinfinite · 07.04.2021"},{"title":"hlop — file utility for Windows | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/hlop/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV hlop by Gagarin File converter with a radial menu, batch processing and local OCR. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 09 DIRECTION: Windows · Files and OCR ← FULL CATALOGUE What it does I built hlop so I wouldn’t have to jump between a pile of programs for routine file operations. Images, audio, video, PDF, documents, archives — everything in one place. Version 1.2.0 includes presets, watched folders and hotkeys. Author page for version 1.2.0 Role and distribution I made the version for Windows 10 1809+ and Windows 11 x64, and the EXE can be downloaded. Some Office and PDF operations require LibreOffice; text recognition uses the languages installed in Windows. Description, requirements and download"},{"title":"Roman Gagarin’s Portfolio — Marketing, Websites, Games | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/","section":"Project","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / SARATOV WORK not promises This is my portfolio: marketing and PR, websites, game media, games, programs and tools. Some projects I did for companies, others I came up with and launched myself. I work from Saratov, and many of the results can be opened right now. SOLUTIONS ↗ BIOGRAPHY ↗ INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECTS AND DEVELOPMENT For each work I made a separate page: what I did, how it is built and where you can see the result. ALL MARKETING / PR MEDIA / WEBSITES GAMES TOOLS FOUND: 14 HIS MAJESTY’S SQUAD · THE EMPEROR'S OWN 01 / 2019–2023 · Marketing / PR / Product The Emperor’s Own · The Emperor's Own At Volga Studios I worked on the game product, marketing and press, prepared the Kickstarter and handled organisational issues. The campaign reached 229 backers and $32 739 in pledged contributions, then it was cancelled. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Kickstarter campaign ↗ 02 / Catalogue / Web project All Indie I built All Indie, my own platform for independent games, programs and digital products. Here my work can not only be read but also tried out. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Open site ↗ 03 / Media / Encyclopedia SNG Games I'm developing SNG Games: news, a catalogue of games, studios and releases, with a focus on the CIS and independent development. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Open site ↗ GAGARIN PANORAMA STUDIO 04 / Commercial product / 360° Gagarin Panorama Studio I built an editor for interactive 360° spaces for games, presentations and virtual routes. The demo can be opened. Using it in a commercial project is something we can agree on separately. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Open editor ↗ TIHAYA VODA 05 / Game / Horror Tihaya Voda I'm making Tihaya Voda, an Arctic horror about exploring a station, the things you find there, and the different ways the story can unfold. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Play ↗ VIDOSIK 06 / Video / Content VIDOSIK At VIDOSIK I built a production process for videos about games, from choosing a topic and writing the script to voice-over, illustrations, editing and publishing. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Watch videos ↗ 07 / Game / Psychological horror AFTER “AFTER” is my horror game about a multi-storey building, a lift and ordinary things that gradually stop being ordinary. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Open game ↗ 08 / Game / Browser MENYALA.exe In “MENYALA.exe” I made a game about trading items and deals: short rounds, negotiations and the gradual rise in value of things. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ Play ↗ 09 / Utility / Windows hlop by Gagarin I built hlop, a program for file conversion, batch processing and text recognition. Version 1.2.0 for Windows. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ BROWSER GAMES AND EXPERIMENTS 10 / Curated selection Browser games and experiments “Atlas of Zero”, “Matrix Operator”, “Durak with O. Zh. Grant”, “The Last Pass” and my other games. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ UTILITIES AND EXTENSIONS 11 / Curated selection Utilities and extensions Programs for files, images, PDFs and tasks. Each one is marked with its publication status and whether a distribution is available. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ GAGARIN PANORAMA FORGE 12 / Panoramas / Production tool Gagarin Panorama Forge I built the 360° panorama processing core for Tihaya Voda and described how it integrates into the game. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ NATIONAL PLATFORM OF DIGITAL PRODUCTS ROS 13 / Analytics / Initiative concept National platform of digital products in Russia I prepared a concept for the infrastructure of the Russian digital products market: the platform's structure, its economic model and supporting materials. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ 14 / 2026 · WebGL / Generative experiment Matter — Generative Study 001 Liquid metal, geometric facets and the breakdown of form. The graphics respond to movement; the full version lets you turn on sound. ABOUT THE PROJECT ↗ OPEN ↗ Early projects and first experience are in the archive: view archive ↗"},{"title":"Materia — interactive WebGL graphics | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/materia/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / LAB / 2026 MATERIA Generative Study 001 “Materia” is my experiment with live graphics: form, light and motion are calculated by code directly in the browser. LAUNCH ORIGINAL ↗ PROJECT PAGE ↗ ← LAB WEBGL / GLSL / BROWSER GENERATIVE STUDY 001 EXPERIMENT / 001 I made “Materia” for the sake of the graphics and the behaviour of form. Later I carried some of its shader techniques over into the accents of this site. Developer: Gagarin Platform: browser All Indie catalogue: from October 21, 2026 ← FULL CATALOGUE Movement is response. Click is impulse. Keys 1–3 change the state. 01 / FLUIDITY 02 / STRUCTURE 03 / DECAY PAUSE What happens on screen The browser calculates the form, light and reflections on the fly. Move the cursor, touch the screen or switch states. Three states I made three modes: “Flow” with smooth movement, the more geometric “Structure”, and “Decay”, where the form deforms more strongly. In the full version I added pause, fullscreen mode and keys 1, 2 and 3 to switch states. On this page you can also change the mode, give the scene an impulse and pause it. Procedural sound The sound is synthesised directly in the browser and is off by default. It can be turned on inside “Materia”; on the portfolio pages nothing plays on its own. How it's used here I put a lightweight version of “Materia” on the home page and in the tools. It lives right among the site's elements, responds to movement and changes state. The text and navigation do not depend on it. If reduced motion is enabled, the form freezes. If the browser doesn't support WebGL, a static image stays in place, and the site remains usable. Open and check Original interactive scene ↗ All Indie project card ↗ I published “Materia” on All Indie on October 21, 2026."},{"title":"MENYALA.exe — browser game about trading items | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/menyala/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV MENYALA.exe Start with something simple and try trading it for something more valuable. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 08 DIRECTION: Game · Browser ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project “MENYALA.exe” is my browser game about trading items and negotiation. You start with almost nothing, bargain, make offers, and gradually work your way up to more expensive items. A short session right in your browser, nothing to install. Trades and negotiations with characters. I published the game on All Indie. View the work Play ↗ Project description ↗ Author card You start with a paperclip. Every visitor has their own interests, so you have to choose items and add-ons, negotiate, and decide whether the deal is worth making. Description and authorship"},{"title":"Operator 911 — text horror | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/operator-911/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Operator 911 A text-based chat horror about the work of an emergency operator and difficult calls. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 14 DIRECTION: Early project · 2020 ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project “Operator 911” is one of my early games. I built a text horror and a web demo so it could be tried without installing, then launched a fundraiser on Planeta.ru and ads on VKontakte. I took the figures from my article of February 12, 2020, where I described this experiment in detail. I set the goal on Planeta.ru at 11 000 ₽. In the end, 3 750 ₽ came in, including all payments. Excluding my own contributions and early payments, other people contributed 1 050 ₽. I calculated this separately in the article. I also tested ads: the CTR was 4.1%, and 3.7% after narrowing the audience. Separate crowdfunding experience The Planeta.ru campaign happened before the Kickstarter run at Volga Studios. The amounts and CTR are in the article from February 12, 2020. I did not include the ad budget in that publication. View the work Article on DTF · 12.02.2020 ↗ Planeta.ru page ↗ Link status The web demo is no longer available. However, my DTF article with the figures and the launch story is still up. On Planeta.ru, the archive sometimes asks for a verification check. Original author review"},{"title":"Gagarin Panorama Forge — 360° panorama processing","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/panorama-forge/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Gagarin Panorama Forge Processing 360° images and integrating panorama fragments into Tihaya Voda. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 12 DIRECTION: Panoramas · Production tool ← FULL CATALOGUE Purpose Forge came out of a specific problem: standard 360° panoramas were limiting scene quality. I built a tool that checks the 2:1 aspect ratio, changes resolution, and works with the image seam. It's built on Python, Pillow, and NumPy, and Real-ESRGAN can be plugged in for upscaling. Public core of Panorama Forge Connection to Tihaya Voda On November 1, 2026, I documented how I integrated the Forge 0.1 core into the production of Tihaya Voda: after processing, a panorama is split into fragments and assembled in the game scene. Integration documentation · 01.11.2026 Role and origin of the code I set the requirements for the tool and decide what the game needs. I write the code, build, and checks together with Codex. I kept the source code and the materials history in the Tihaya Voda README. Game README ↗ Source code Verified scope For now, Forge is a core and a set of scripts inside Tihaya Voda. Scaling and fragment assembly have already been tested locally. I haven't yet run full 8K processing on a GPU, and there is no separate installer yet. Documentation: limitations and verification"},{"title":"Gagarin Panorama Studio — 360° space editor","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/panorama-studio/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Gagarin Panorama Studio An editor for interactive 360° spaces for games, presentations, and virtual routes. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 04 DIRECTION: Product · 360° ← FULL CATALOGUE What Panorama Studio does I created Panorama Studio to turn ordinary 360° panoramas into full interactive spaces. In the editor, you can place objects, create transitions, link actions to events, and assemble browser scenes. I built the panorama and transition point workflow. I added objects, dialogues, triggers, and scripted events. I build interactive scenes and standalone web projects in the editor. Open demo I've opened the editor demo to everyone, so you can look at the interface and try the features. I discuss commercial licensing and implementation separately. Try Panorama Studio ↗ Commercial use I can adapt Panorama Studio for a virtual tour, an interactive presentation, a browser story, or a game scene. What needs to be reworked will be decided based on the task. Licensing and delivery of the editor for a specific project are available on request. Setting up scenes, interactive points, and logic. Integration of a finished project into a website or browser product. If you want to use Panorama Studio in your project, write to me. We can discuss features, implementation and licensing. Discuss licensing by email ↗ Write on Telegram ↗ Project materials I described how I built the editor in detail in a publication. Part of the code and technical materials are already open; custom builds and implementation are discussed separately. Creation story on DTF ↗ Technical documentation ↗"},{"title":"AFTER — psychological horror | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/posle/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV AFTER A story set in a multi-storey building, where ordinary things gradually stop being ordinary. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 07 DIRECTION: Game · Psychological horror ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project «AFTER» is my horror about a multi-storey building, a lift and strange events on the floors. What matters most to me here is atmosphere, sound, exploration, encounters with residents and a story that can be played through to the end. The story unfolds through the building and the events happening inside it. Dialogue and interaction with characters. The game can be opened in a browser. View the work Project page ↗ Project description ↗ Published version In version 7.1 you can choose the order of trips between floors yourself. Progress is saved in the browser; Russian and English languages are included. Game card and current version"},{"title":"SNG Games — gaming news and CIS game catalogue | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/sng-games/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV SNG Games Gaming news and a catalogue of projects from the CIS and independent development. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 03 DIRECTION: Gaming media · Encyclopedia ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project SNG Games is my gaming media project and reference guide to games from the CIS and independent teams. I made a card for each game, separate pages for studios and publishers, and gathered releases into a calendar. I select and publish gaming industry news. I develop the catalogue of games, studios, publishers and releases. I handle data, SEO and distribution of materials. View the work Open SNG Games ↗ Telegram ↗ Zen ↗ Connection to the author's platform SNG Games is my separate project about games. The news is linked to the catalogue: from an article you can go to the game, its developer and the release date. All Indie's author on SNG Games Public site"},{"title":"Tihaya Voda — Arctic horror | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/tihaya-voda/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Tihaya Voda A horror about an Arctic station, isolation and what is found beneath the ice. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 05 DIRECTION: Game · Arctic horror ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project I'm making «Tihaya Voda» as a large Arctic horror, not a short demo. A polar station, exploration of the territory, documents, sound, story discoveries, tasks and several endings. There is a browser version you can try. The source code and development history are in an open repository. Plot, quests, interactive scenes and graphics — I'm still working on all of it. View the work Play in browser ↗ Source code on GitHub ↗ What is published in the repository The game is still in development. The repository contains source code, a browser build, the Studio editor and tools. Some of the graphics and video are still temporary; I'm also still refining the sound and voice-over. Game README ↗ Documentation for panoramic fragments"},{"title":"Utilities and extensions — byGagarin programs","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/utilities/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV Utilities and extensions Here are my programs for files, documents and everyday tasks, plus a few browser extensions. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 11 DIRECTION: Author's tools · byGagarin ← FULL CATALOGUE byGagarin Utilities Here I've collected programs for Windows and Chromium extensions. Each work has a description, requirements and a download link where a build is published. Where there is no file yet, I've said so. I last checked the list on 17 November 2026. Author's platform hlop by Gagarin I built file conversion, batch processing and local text recognition in hlop. Windows · version 1.2.0 · EXE published Description and download ↗ Gagarin Audio Converter Audio converter to common formats. Windows · portable EXE published Description and download ↗ Gagarin Image Converter Image converter with resizing and transparency removal. Windows · EXE published Description and download ↗ Gagarin Image to PDF Builds a PDF document from images. Windows · version 1.0.0 · EXE published Description and download ↗ Gagarin Tasks A standalone app for personal tasks. Windows · EXE published Description and download ↗ Startup Cleaner by Gagarin Windows autorun utility with quarantine and action log. Windows · beta · available through an external service, via the author's listing Description and download ↗ Folder Cleaner Searches for temporary files in the selected folder. Windows · beta · download file not available Description and download ↗ Flash Drive Sorter Sorts files on a USB drive by type and date. Windows · MVP · download file not available Description and download ↗ Gagarin Document Converter Converts office documents and helps prepare PDFs. Windows · description published, no download file available right now Description and download ↗ Extensions for personal time limits I built a series of beta extensions for Chromium to limit the time spent on certain websites. The user sets the limit themselves; once it's reached, a restriction screen appears. Installation is manual, and settings are stored locally. antiBoosty antiDTF antiReddit antiTelegram antiVC antiYouTube"},{"title":"VIDOSIK — video production about games | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/projects/vidosik/","section":"Project","priority":1,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 02 / CASE / SARATOV VIDOSIK From choosing a game to a finished video: script, voiceover, illustrations, editing and publishing. ← HOME INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU PROJECT / 06 DIRECTION: Video · Content production ← FULL CATALOGUE About the project VIDOSIK is my video project about computer game stories. I run the whole process: choosing the game, script, voiceover, illustrations, editing shorts and long-form videos, and publishing. We automate a significant part of the routine work. I publish short story recaps for YouTube Shorts. I put together full-length videos and longer versions of the stories. I built my own production pipeline and editorial plan. View the work YouTube channel ↗ Boosty ↗ Public information dashboard On a separate page I show released episodes and the queue of upcoming videos. The dashboard opens without registration. Open dashboard How the dashboard works ↗"},{"title":"Publications and interviews by Roman Gagarin | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/publications/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 05 / SARATOV PUBLICATIONS and interviews Here I've gathered my articles, interviews and publications on marketing, promoting indie games and development. It also includes materials where journalists interviewed me. All of them link to the originals. TO HOME PAGE ↗ INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU Author materials and interviews 12.02.2020 · DTF · Author article Crowdfunding for indie games in Russia. Why doesn’t it work? I broke down my own experience with “Operator 911” on Planeta.ru: the web demo, the advertising, and the money we actually managed to raise. 18.02.2020 · Igrozhory / Soundstream · Podcast / interview Guest: Roman Naberushkin I was invited to talk about “The Emperor’s Own”, our team, and how we worked on the game in our spare time. 07.12.2020 · DTF · Author article A guide to zero-budget marketing? I wrote about free game promotion: first contacts with the press, small bloggers, and working with the community. 09.12.2020 · vc.ru · Author article About bloggers, influencers and journalists for indie games I explained how I made first contact with journalists and gaming bloggers, and what usually stops people from simply reaching out to them. 09.02.2025 · DTF · Author publication Announcement of the book “Moving Indie” I talked about the release of “Moving Indie”, the work on the book, and where to find it. 24.10.2026 · DTF · Development diary Gagarin Panorama Studio: an editor’s story I showed how I built Gagarin Panorama Studio: scenes, objects, events, dialogue, sound and standalone HTML export. I also talked about working with AI. 24.10.2026 · DEV Community · Author development diary Hello DEV! I'm building indie games and the tools behind them On DEV I wrote in English about Hollywood Massacre and Gagarin Panorama Studio. I also left a link to All Indie. Mentions in the games press My comments on “The Emperor’s Own” ran on DSOGaming and Twinfinite. Rozetked and CoreMission wrote about the project’s launch on Kickstarter. 07.04.2021 · DSOGaming The Emperor’s Own: Alpha Teaser is now available for free on Steam John Papadopoulos wrote about the alpha teaser of The Emperor’s Own and included my comment from Volga Studios. 07.04.2021 · Twinfinite Open-World RPG The Emperor’s Own Looks Promising in First Footage; Free Alpha Demo Available Now Alex Gibson covered the first footage and alpha demo of The Emperor’s Own. The article includes my comment about the game. 05.11.2020 · Rozetked “The Russian Witcher” The Emperor's Own launches on Kickstarter Denis Guryanov wrote about our Kickstarter and the free demo. 06.11.2020 · CoreMission A Kickstarter campaign to fund The Emperor’s Own has launched Alexander Koloskov wrote about the launch of our campaign, the goal of $100,000, and the first chapter of the game being available to play."},{"title":"Marketer and developer in Saratov — Roman Gagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/services/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"SOLUTIONS as needed I'm Roman Gagarin. I work in marketing, PR, SEO, website and digital product development, and automation. I work from Saratov with local and remote projects. Experience Marketing, people and processes. I have led Advertising and PR at Teleport, marketing at Medical Di-Center and digital marketing at Apriori, and worked as CMO at Volga Studios. Budgets, campaign plans, team tasks, contractor coordination and reporting. In-house marketing work included Tilda websites, SEO, social targeting, reviews and Telegram/WhatsApp bots. Download CV · PDF (Russian) Full work history 01 / What challenges Situations, not price list. My work doesn’t stop at setting up ads or writing code. I can look at a task from a marketing standpoint, help with the product, build a website or automate a process. For projects in other cities, I work remotely. 01 Internet marketing · SEO · PR Clients aren't coming in, and ads don't pay off I look at the offer, the audience, the website and the ads. I check where people come from and at which step they drop off. Then we decide what to fix. Marketing and acquisition channel audit Positioning, strategy and media plan SEO, content, PR and community work Funnel analytics and clear reporting Deliverables: a map of problems, priorities, an action plan and, if needed, setup and management of the chosen channels. Volga Studios case ↗ 02 Product · Research · Launch I have an idea, but it's unclear how to turn it into a product I help define who the product is for, what problem it solves, and what really needs to be done in the first working version. From concept to a testable prototype and launch. Analysis of the audience, competitors and usage scenarios Product structure and user flows Feature prioritisation and technical specification Prototype, launch and development plan Deliverables: an agreed concept, a clear scope of work, a prototype or a working product. All Indie ↗ 03 Website development · Tools · Integrations You need a website or tool that actually works I build websites, catalogues and small applications. Where a ready-made solution fits, I use it. Where custom code is needed, I build it and check it with AI. Working results matter more to me than complexity for its own sake. Structure, content, interface and SEO foundation Catalogues, search, forms and user scenarios Integrations, APIs and automation of repetitive operations WordPress customisation, small plugins and integrations as needed Publication, testing and handover Deliverables: a published website, application or agreed tool. I also develop and set up 360° scenes built with Panorama Studio. SNG Games ↗ 04 Processes · Content · Teams The work relies on manual tasks and constant reminders I look at the whole process: who does what, where information gets lost, which operations repeat, and where automation is genuinely worth the complexity. Process mapping and division of responsibilities Editorial and production pipelines Service integrations, bots and checkpoints Documentation and result review Deliverables: a simpler workflow, instructions and tools that work. VIDOSIK ↗ 05 Non-standard and mixed tasks It's not even clear yet how to name the problem We don't start with choosing a service, but with a conversation about the situation. We separate symptoms from causes, define the constraints, and decide what you can do yourself and where you need specialists. Initial review and task definition Research of options and risks Building a plan and a team if needed Implementation control and result review Deliverables: a clear problem statement and the next sensible step, even if it doesn't turn into a joint project. Start with a description ↗ 02 / How I work No empty promises. First I assess the task and its constraints. Scope, timelines, cost and the form of collaboration are discussed once it's clear what needs to be done. 01 / UNDERSTAND Understand the context Goal, current situation, constraints and previous attempts. 02 / DEFINE Find the cause Separate the symptom from the problem and choose an approach. 03 / AGREE Describe the work Result, scope, roles, timelines and budget before the start. 04 / DELIVER Get it done Build, test and hand over something you can actually use. Have a task? Let's start with it. Describe the situation in your own words. You don't need to prepare a technical specification or know in advance which specialist you need. Write up the task description See the work ↗"},{"title":"Programs and Tools — Roman Gagarin | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/tools/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"BYGAGARIN / 04 / SARATOV LAB in action Here I've gathered my programs and experiments: Panorama Studio, browser tools, utilities and generative graphics. Some of them can be launched right away. MY PROJECTS ↗ CALCULATORS ↗ PANORAMA STUDIO ↗ INDEPENDENT AUTHOR'S BUREAU GENERATIVE STUDY 001 / WEBGL REAL MATTER. Run your finger or cursor across it and the shape will respond. Click to give it an impulse, or choose another state. 01 / FLUIDITY 02 / STRUCTURE 03 / DECAY PAUSE OPEN FULL ORIGINAL ↗ Movement is response. Click is impulse. Keys 1–3 change the state. 01 / Tools in use Open and check. An editor, media, games and programs. I use some of them every day and keep improving others. You can open them and check. 01 360° · Web tool Gagarin Panorama Studio I built an editor for 360° spaces with scenes, transitions, objects and events. The demo is open, and I discuss commercial use and implementation in person. Open editor ↗ · Project history 02 Catalog · Web platform All Indie My platform for independent games, utilities and digital projects. Cards, categories and search. Open All Indie ↗ 03 Media · Database SNG Games My games media project: a catalog of games, studios, publishers and releases, plus editorial pieces. Open SNG Games ↗ 04 Windows · Utility hlop by Gagarin My file converter: batch processing, presets, a radial menu and local OCR. Page and download ↗ 05 Game · Browser horror “Tihaya Voda” My Arctic horror about a station, story discoveries and interactive scenes. Play the game ↗ · GitHub ↗ 06 Development tool Gagarin Panorama Forge A tool I built for processing panoramas and preparing image fragments. Description, limitations and source files ↗ 07 Generative graphics · WebGL / GLSL Matter — Generative Study 001 My procedural scene with three states: “Fluidity”, “Structure” and “Decay”. It responds to the cursor and clicks, and sound is off by default. I carried some of its techniques over into the site design. Run the original ↗ · About the project ↗ 02 / A small calculation Check an advertising funnel. Enter your own numbers. The calculator shows basic indicators. It does not forecast anything and does not replace analytics. Ad budget, ₽ Leads Sales Revenue, ₽ Cost per lead 500 ₽ Cost per customer 5 000 ₽ ROAS 4,0× JavaScript is required for the calculation. Example: a budget of 10,000 ₽, 20 leads, 2 sales and 40,000 ₽ in revenue give a cost per lead of 500 ₽, a cost per customer of 5,000 ₽ and a ROAS of 4×. All 16 calculators: ROI, ROMI, margin, break-even point, LTV and more ↗ Need a tool for your task? Sometimes a ready-made tool is enough. If there isn't one, I can design and build a custom one for your task. Describe the task View case studies ↗"},{"title":"Website development in Saratov — Roman Gagarin | byGagarin","url":"/bygagarin-portfolio/en/web-development-saratov/","section":"Page","priority":8,"text":"DEVELOPMENT websites in Saratov I am Roman Gagarin. I develop websites, catalogs, web tools and interactive products. I work from Saratov: I plan the structure and SEO, build the interface, test it and take it through to launch. 01 / What I build Not just a page. A working tool. I build websites in Saratov and for clients in other regions. It can be a small site, a large catalog or a standalone web service. I don't overcomplicate a system for the sake of elegant architecture: what matters most is that it solves the problem. 01 Websites · Structure · SEO A site should explain, be found and work I design the structure and navigation, and build the pages, content and interface. I account for mobile devices, accessibility, speed and search engine requirements. Company websites and personal portfolios Catalogs, project and publication sections Semantic structure, metadata and internal linking Contact forms and user flows Result: a published site with a clear structure, working navigation and an SEO foundation. 02 WordPress · APIs · Integrations When a ready-made platform isn't enough I improve existing websites and build small tools for specific processes. I use ready-made solutions where they fit and write custom code where it is justified. WordPress improvements and small plugins Service integrations and APIs Search, filtering, catalogs and forms Automation of repetitive actions and editorial processes Result: a site or tool that solves a specific work task. 03 Interactive · 360° · WebGL Web products you can interact with I build browser games, interactive graphics and tools for 360° spaces. These are not just presentation effects: such projects have state, logic, events and a user flow. Interactive 360° scenes and virtual tours Browser games and prototypes Generative graphics and WebGL experiments Exports and standalone web versions Result: a working interactive product you can open and check. Gagarin Panorama Studio ↗ 04 Programs · Windows · Utilities Small programs for specific tasks I develop utilities and applications that remove unnecessary manual steps: file processing, format conversion, text recognition and other practical workflows. hlop by Gagarin ↗ Other utilities ↗ 02 / Published work You can open it and check it. My portfolio includes working websites, catalogues, programs, editors and games. Most of them can be opened and tested, not just viewed as mockups. 01 Catalogue · Website · Search All Indie All Indie is my platform for games, programs and digital projects. I built the catalogue, cards, categories and navigation. All Indie case study ↗ Open site ↗ 02 Gaming media · Encyclopedia SNG Games At SNG Games I develop a gaming news site and a catalogue of CIS projects: games, studios, publishers, releases, search and editorial workflows. SNG Games case study ↗ Open site ↗ 03 Custom editor · 360° Gagarin Panorama Studio With Panorama Studio I built an editor for interactive 360° spaces: scenes, transitions, objects, events and export for the browser. About the project ↗ Open demo ↗ 04 Interactive graphics · WebGL Matter \"Matter\" is my experiment with generative graphics that react to movement and switch between states. About the project ↗ 03 / How I work From the brief to publication. I have no interest in building complex architecture just because I can. If a task can be solved more simply and reliably, I choose the simpler approach. Results first, technology second. 01 Scoping Understanding the task Users, scenarios, constraints, content and acceptance criteria. 02 Solution Choose an approach and build Structure, interface, data, integrations and the functionality required, without unnecessary layers. 03 Testing Publish and verify Testing of core scenarios, responsiveness, bug fixing, publication and handover. I use AI as a working tool for code, builds and checks. Ideas, task definition, product decisions, content and the final result remain my responsibility. Commercial experience Websites as part of marketing. At Apriori, I built promotional websites on Tilda, handled SEO and launched Telegram and WhatsApp bots for customers. At Teleport, I made websites for projects; at Hotel Areal, I administered the website and updated its content. Download CV · PDF (Russian) Roles and dates 04 / Geography Saratov. All of Russia. I live and work in Saratov. I build websites and digital tools for local projects and for remote teams in other regions. If you need a website in Saratov, a catalogue, an interactive product or a useful web tool, write to me. A finished technical brief is not required: we will first work out what needs to be done. Meeting address by prior arrangement: Saratov, Bolshaya Sadovaya St., 141"}];
